From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:27:32 +0300
Subject: renderergl2: r_glslLazy, build each GLSL program at its first use

Even without the bone and FBO variants, every program the renderer might pick is compiled at
start (54 with OpenArena's settings), though a map draws with far fewer. With r_glslLazy 1,
GLSL_InitGPUShaders only records how to build each program (its defines, attributes and sampler
units) and the first GLSL_BindProgram or uniform set builds it: a short stall the first time a
variant is drawn, instead of all of them at start. Kept programs (r_glslKeepPrograms) are still
taken at start, so a map load after the menu only builds what the menu didn't use. Default 0.

diff --git a/code/renderergl2/tr_glsl.c b/code/renderergl2/tr_glsl.c
--- a/code/renderergl2/tr_glsl.c
+++ b/code/renderergl2/tr_glsl.c
